{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015846-dark-eras-how-to-perceive-time","id":1015846,"title":"[Dark Eras] How to perceive time?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-11T14:28:49-08:00","id":1015846,"title":"[Dark Eras] How to perceive time?","content":"I think it\u2019s interesting video on how we should perceive events and settings in Chronicles of Darkness history context. I know probably OPP will stick to classical BCE/CE dates still, but just see this thought process of cultures emerges. It also interesting with intersecting such events as Atlantis ( or maybe few of them? ) or Pangea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=czgOWmtGVGs\" data-code=\"czgOWmtGVGs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/czgOWmtGVGs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T21:12:12-08:00","id":1015973,"title":"","content":"I am not able to watch that video where I am, but based on what you said, I can say that I try to use the appropriate calendar depending on the setting of my story. For example, I would use a sidereal calendar if it was based in ancient egypt.<br /> <br /> There are other things to consider, such as the precession of the equinoxes, the fact that solar and lunar cycles are not commensurate, and other factors such as the gross innaccuracies of the Greek and Julian calendars in real history ( How they made such an amateur mistake like doing a leap year every three years instead of four, especially considering it came from the Egyptians who were accurate, I don't know. But just wanted to give a concrete example.) I like to keep all the mistakes made by the culture and generally reflect with how advanced they are with astronomy and mathematics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T21:24:53-08:00","id":1015977,"title":"","content":"The video suggests a global calendar based on human cultural development, that effectively just adds 10,000 years to the Gregorian date (so it would currently be 12016 of the human era). It dates from the earliest known stone temple ruins in Anatolia.<br /> <br /> (note: we only assume it's a &quot;temple&quot; because that's archaeologist for &quot;we have no idea what this was actually for&quot;. Religion is the go to answer for anything they can't figure out a utilitarian explanation of. Keep that in mind whenever there's a discussion of &quot;ceremonial&quot; tools, or writing that can't be deciphered but clearly isn't an inventory list so they assume it served a spiritual purpose)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T21:37:08-08:00","id":1015981,"title":"","content":"Neat! I don't think it's particularly relevant for dark eras games because it isn't really pertinent in most such games to recognize the relative modernity of what we consider human history. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1715_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1715\" data-vbnamecard=\"1715\">Ostarion</a> pointed out, using calendars contemporary to the era being played in seems more useful <i>for the purposes of a historical game</i>. But, in general it's a fascinating concept.<br /> <br /> Also, anyone else notice the DHMIS clock?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T21:41:22-08:00","id":1015982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015846-dark-eras-how-to-perceive-time?p=1015981#post1015981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, anyone else notice the DHMIS clock?</div> </div> </div> </div>MEH! MEH! MEH! MEH! MEH! MEH! MEH!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T23:56:41-08:00","id":1016005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015846-dark-eras-how-to-perceive-time?p=1015981#post1015981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat! I don't think it's particularly relevant for dark eras games because it isn't really pertinent in most such games to recognize the relative modernity of what we consider human history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beside idea to add 10000 years to Gregorian date as cool thing to do ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) - I posted and connected it to <b>Dark Eras</b> books, highlighting to show that 'Christ Era' is not start of civilization as we know it. That those processes started with beginning of Stone Age and some interesting stories can be told before what we call 'Western civilization'.<br /> <br /> It's in the same vain as how now is looked term of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Ages_(historiography)#Modern_academic_use\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Ages</a> - there were not only in early Middle Ages one ( circa V to X century CE ), but, for example, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greek_Dark_Ages\" target=\"_blank\">Bronze Age Collapse</a> is taken in consideration as next 'Dark Ages' era in modern writing - and it's only one of many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-12-2016, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T00:09:34-08:00","id":1016011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015846-dark-eras-how-to-perceive-time?p=1015977#post1015977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(note: we only assume it's a &quot;temple&quot; because that's archaeologist for &quot;we have no idea what this was actually for&quot;. Religion is the go to answer for anything they can't figure out a utilitarian explanation of. Keep that in mind whenever there's a discussion of &quot;ceremonial&quot; tools, or writing that can't be deciphered but clearly isn't an inventory list so they assume it served a spiritual purpose)</div> </div> </div> </div>It strangely reminds me about Times Before phenomena in <b>Mage</b> - 'Oh, those ruins <i>must be</i> of our Atlantean forefathers great civilization! It surely was for something benign...' &lt;Dropping of Bounds cell wards&gt; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T10:15:14-08:00","id":1016146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015846-dark-eras-how-to-perceive-time?p=1016005#post1016005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beside idea to add 10000 years to Gregorian date as cool thing to do ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) - I posted and connected it to <b>Dark Eras</b> books, highlighting to show that 'Christ Era' is not start of civilization as we know it. That those processes started with beginning of Stone Age and some interesting stories can be told before what we call 'Western civilization'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, which I don't think is a particularly important thing for dark era games. Why does it matter to a game of Requiem for Rome that CE (which actually stands for current era, not christ era) isn't really the start of civilization? The development of humanity isn't really a subject these games focus on.<br /> <br /> It's still cool, and relevant to real life historians. But not to roleplaying games set in historical periods, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T14:03:09-08:00","id":1016231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015846-dark-eras-how-to-perceive-time?p=1016146#post1016146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, which I don't think is a particularly important thing for dark era games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just add that we have only one era that is significantly out from the Common Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T15:49:02-08:00","id":1016287,"title":"","content":"And CE NEVER has meant the beginning of civilization, so I dont see any problem about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T16:08:27-08:00","id":1016300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1015846-dark-eras-how-to-perceive-time?p=1016287#post1016287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And CE NEVER has meant the beginning of civilization, so I dont see any problem about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I get where the proposal is coming from - presenting everything from 1 CE on as the current era creates a subconscious perception that everything before that point is ancient. But, when you look at it in the context of the entirety of human history, 1 CE wasn't all that long ago. Pushing year 0 back would help make it more clear that 2016 years isn't such a long time on a historical scale - on the contrary, it's only a tiny fraction of our lifespan as a species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-12-2016, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}